# What the mini runs that Homebrew does not bring, pinned by version and
# checksum.
#
#   name  version  sha256  url
#
# A line whose url is a .pkg (https) is installed on the mini:
# scripts/mini/setup and the Maintenance run download it, compare the
# checksum and only then install it; a Deploy touches none.
#
# macvdmtool is the reset tool, the lab's fork with a required, strictly
# parsed --rid. Its version is the commit, its checksum the sha256 of
# `git archive --format=tar <commit>`, its url the repository. The release
# workflow's macOS job checks both and builds it (release/reset-tool.sh);
# it reaches the mini in the server bundle, never by a download there.
macvdmtool d57c4850b386fea7c0c7e406addde2703a5f9f29 2f84325a8066947137769b100bfd1f5c0cd9b506046b74a2e4214e9e52049701 https://github.com/omacom/macvdmtool
#
# container is Apple's, the Builder's VMs run in it. The checksum is the one
# GitHub records for the release's signed package.
container 1.7.1 b6739caf3d47ca53a78f1a7edf32521420a75c7941838c3cefa75f30b80f5a97 https://github.com/apple/container/releases/download/1.7.1/container-1.7.1-installer-signed.pkg
